        "original_id": "4907e230-439a-5a44-a370-5f6c81455d15",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Anaïs Nin, Odysseas Elytis\n- Places: France, Greece\n- Roles: essayist, memoirist\n- Concepts: romantic modernism\n- Awards: Nobel Prize in Literature\n\nFacts:\n- Anaïs Nin was born as Angela Anaïs Juana Antolina Rosa Edelmira Nin y Culmell on February 21, 1903.\n- Anaïs Nin was an essayist and memoirist born to Cuban parents in France, where she was also raised.\n- Odysseas Elytis, the pen name of Odysseas Alepoudellis, was born on November 2, 1911.\n- Odysseas Elytis was regarded as a major exponent of romantic modernism in Greece and internationally.\n- Odysseas Elytis was awarded the 1979 Nobel Prize in Literature.\n- Anaïs Nin died on January 14, 1977.\n- Odysseas Elytis died on March 18, 1996.",
